{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.219789Z","id":"be9d8cfbfcf1df93df0cbe72d519dfdee627dbb283e0d45e24cc929fedae2149","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 10 gives GET /api/me/bot without the caller's role, and the shell needs it to show Admin (web/shell/src/bot/HeaderBot.svelte, web/shell/src/people/People.svelte) and to make the role select owner-only (web/shell/src/bot/AdminPeople.svelte). Without it, web/shell/src/bot/me.ts myRole takes the owner's shell (it holds the token) as the owner and anyone else as a member, so a hosted admin who is not the owner sees no Admin link. The server's GET /api/me/bot should carry role: owner|admin|member.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"f6285a18ba965a7f00a57b75e899e2f7319a23fc1772d5d92410d1ff79398b4f"},"summary":"The shell reads the caller's role from GET /api/me/bot (role), which the ClaxBot spec's section 10 does not list","tags":["claxbot","api-shape","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.219851Z","id":"098474dd1482f440bba49dea59f7e6a489beb643124f21010acd19eb92aeb6f5","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 10 names routes and fields; web/shell/src/bot/api.ts fixes what it leaves open: the run events' data (step_started {step}, turn_delta {step, text}, script {step, title, code}, call {step, call:{op,target,ok,ms,error}}, step_done {step, run?}, run_end {run}); BotRun and BotStep; GET /api/bot/runs?artifact= as {runs}; POST /api/bot/runs answering {run}; GET /api/admin/people as a bare array; AdminUsage (paid_milli, free_milli, revenue_micro_usd, cost_micro_usd, free_cost_micro_usd, by_person, by_line); GET /api/settings as {fields: {dotted.name: {value, source, editable, restart_required, secret?}}} and PUT /api/settings {values}; GET /api/me/usage as {week, runs, totals}; GET /api/audit/<seq> as the event with body at top level; AuditEvent.actor and on_behalf_of as {id, name}; Provider.caps by config name and Provider.sources by dotted field name (key, base_url, models.default, caps.max_steps); CostLine.fixed_milli for the harness fee; POST /api/artifacts:new with build answering run {id}; week.weekly_milli as the whole allowance (free tier plus lift). A server that differs breaks the screens silently; the unit fixtures in web/shell/src/bot/fixtures.ts are the reference.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"56125875da2528464cc02f2f4db7980590faa04522a48f6dc7550541cb9f3d50"},"summary":"The shapes the shell reads beyond the ClaxBot spec's section 10 are its own choices, for the server to match","tags":["claxbot","api-shape","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/send.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.220827Z","id":"7f0ab3a2885ae987b356d12e699c93946c416b5c2f014d0ad78c1ab32e32d644","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte sends to ClaxBot through POST /api/bot/runs {thread_ids, artifact_id} (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 10), which has no note, so a note typed in the selection bar before a send to ClaxBot is not sent. Either the route takes note, or the send goes through POST /api/artifacts/<id>/threads:send with to: claxbot and the run is found with GET /api/bot/runs?artifact=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":76}},"summary":"A batch sent to ClaxBot drops the selection bar's note","tags":["claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/UsageBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.220969Z","id":"52813151092b4e5ed43434c6bd91b48d4e452f14583c686d7620ef1f472ca28e","body":{"detail":"The exhausted banner's button reveals a sentence pointing at Admin, People and flags. ClaxBot's API has no route to ask for a lift (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 10), and a member may not list the admins. A request could go to the admins' inbox as an approval request does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"05cdedfd403448ba9fb0047b7b239d79a41f49a977031cc15889a992779630c6"},"summary":"Ask an admin for a lift only says where an admin grants one; nothing reaches an admin","tags":["claxbot","revisit:a route to ask admins for a lift","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AuditPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.221106Z","id":"f909af75887bd4d4bc1cbae936949ee03a375a9ddbd56eec467a4c91d72e7dbd","body":{"detail":"GET /api/toolpath/export is owner only (docs/contract.md, Export; crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs owner_reads_history). The audit page offers the button to everyone and shows the refusal; the ClaxBot spec's section 9.2 lets admins see all events. Either the export takes admins (and a person's own events), or the button shows for the owner alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"29703db3532ee18bab40493c77fc7e632478532512f2a9b107e212b9854f2fae"},"summary":"Export Toolpath is the owner's route: an admin who is not the owner, and anyone else, is refused","tags":["claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/RunPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.221281Z","id":"caf81af5bdfa42b78a1c012dd88e92fd6f33f486429cc1e4b0f200157ecc2354","body":{"detail":"The panel links a stopped run's unpublished draft (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.3) to run.draft.url, a field section 10 does not define. The existing agent drafts open in the artifact view (web/shell/src/view/drafts.ts, ArtifactController.showDraftOf); if the server keeps a run's draft as the agent claxbot's draft, the link could be the view's own Show draft instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"199b12bdcb6daff4855bf0009a4b41bf8930eef1300b41d10a961d0ab437fc70"},"summary":"Open the draft needs the run's draft.url from the server","tags":["claxbot","api-shape","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AuditPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.283915Z","id":"ce1c30bf1ee6dddc9d8b2ee2f08e466ba52f3a5ffb91fe88931935d386097ad7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4a5024bf","summary":"Export Toolpath now shows only when GET /api/me/bot says can_export (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 10); web/shell/src/bot/pages.test.ts 'Audit' and 'Audit's export' pass under just web-test","supersedes":"f909af75887bd4d4bc1cbae936949ee03a375a9ddbd56eec467a4c91d72e7dbd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.301979Z","id":"6dd768947ed2b9d692fa084efdf8e8a48fbd8e4911e2d192aec41ce79038e94a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4a5024bf","summary":"GET /api/me/bot's role is now part of the spec's section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md), which the server is built to","supersedes":"be9d8cfbfcf1df93df0cbe72d519dfdee627dbb283e0d45e24cc929fedae2149","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.319772Z","id":"e2f803717075b14cf9b2aa484b17c55207350a4c59fbbd940dc24ae2cd6fc2d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4a5024bf","summary":"Every shape the shell reads is now written into the spec's section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md), including the run events' SSE ids and Last-Event-ID resume, and the settings route as crates/clax-server/src/routes/settings.rs answers","supersedes":"098474dd1482f440bba49dea59f7e6a489beb643124f21010acd19eb92aeb6f5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/RunPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.338840Z","id":"12a378b41789fb43afe19f21687eabd6a2f6a9ad4aa1d73e7090aa2d8322f735","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4a5024bf","summary":"The run's draft {url} is now part of GET /api/bot/runs/<id> in the spec's section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md)","supersedes":"caf81af5bdfa42b78a1c012dd88e92fd6f33f486429cc1e4b0f200157ecc2354","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:46:40.068472Z","id":"c4c80a522418e699abcebece2647612af5138d94094b314cba5f557d0c32e5f1","body":{"detail":"The elapsed time is the browser's Date.now() minus the step's started_at from the daemon, so a browser clock ahead of the daemon's by minutes shows a turn as running for minutes (one behind shows 0:00); the reel's camera, whose page clock is days ahead, shows thousands of minutes (web/reel/vignettes/claxbot.ts sets its page clock back for this). The branch that reads s.input ('Writing “title” · N lines') never fires: the events route drops tool-input deltas (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs panel_event, turn_delta of a type other than text answers None), so the panel shows 'Thinking · m:ss' while ClaxBot writes a script. Options: time the turn from when the browser first heard it, or send the daemon's now with the run; send tool-input deltas to the run's owner, or drop the branch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"126294d900e3db479bfaa228d02f54a03260ae5c75b4322de16e89ee50b19ef8"},"summary":"turnActivity times a turn from the daemon's clock to the browser's, and its 'Writing …' branch never runs","tags":["claxbot","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:32:49.488508Z","id":"db9fc50fb07e8ff102c5d5f10995aad66f86214724656b6a6199e7ae0d0973df","body":{"detail":"POST /api/admin/pricing/models relabels all four lines with `name` (the model ID when absent), so an Edit must send the name back or 'Claude Sonnet 5.5 input tokens' becomes 'claude-sonnet-5-5 input tokens'. The pricing view carries no model name, so the page parses it from the label; a change to the store's '{name} {what} tokens' format silently falls back to the catalog listing's name or the model ID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"4d4ee3766d9801e88de64de8cde9b158f54cb95ff48c7cd385f203ca4c81c251"},"suggested_fix":"Give each entry of `models` in pricing_view (crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs) a `name`, or let the POST keep the lines' labels when `name` is left out, and drop the parsing.","summary":"nameOf recovers a model's display name by stripping ' input tokens' from its input line's label, coupling the page to the label format of Store::set_model_rates and seed_cost_lines (crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs)","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:32:49.488678Z","id":"fac9fc2147ac2c1b6196fff08982e7b55030e8e10ee822afb427fdb6896cfb3a","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":132},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"b4952b8816c2dc5902128f71e42eff4a435daac6389687215d17fc4505abb0d8"},"suggested_fix":"Expose the token margin in GET /api/admin/pricing (for example `token_margin_bp`) and start RateCard from it.","summary":"TOKEN_MARGIN_BP (4000) is copied from crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs TOKEN_MARGIN_BP; a new rate card in the admin UI starts from this copy and drifts if the store's changes","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:32:49.488736Z","id":"640b22a586f390846449fadd6d4eba2e978649df58019630087ab8cafa41b811","body":{"detail":"The page says where the model's tokens resolve now, so the effect is visible, but restoring the card means retyping it from the audit log.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"33b09a322de2bd7c3006461bece703bfdb2a86e4c3fe993bbcf2199678ae7eba"},"summary":"Remove deletes a model's rate card on one click, without a confirmation; the rates set by hand are gone (the audit log keeps them as admin.cost_line deletes)","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.403071Z","id":"a4c083eaf3673774594153819ad746fad5720b85f1c741356aee8eb02afca7cb","body":{"detail":"save() checks only `busy`; act() and add() check only `mBusy`. Failure: edit a card and click 'Save rates', then click the page's Save before the POST answers. The PUT sends p.lines as last read (line 59); if it lands after the POST, Store::replace_pricing writes the old token lines back (the card's change is reverted) or, for a model just added with 'Add the model' or 'Look up and price', deletes its four lines (a line left out is deleted). The page then shows whichever response arrives last, which may not be what the database holds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"890f041db2a6981d45046d170293ede466be5f7c460dd761dd40db5fe66dd1da"},"suggested_fix":"Use one busy flag for every write on the page (or have save() return while mBusy and act()/add() while busy), and add a test that clicks Save while a POST /api/admin/pricing/models is pending and checks no PUT is sent.","summary":"Save does not wait for a rate-card action in flight (and act() does not wait for Save), so the PUT can carry the token lines read before a card POST and undo it","tags":["review","pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.403197Z","id":"dfdb87020b421fb18db0e82cb9bb4ab453f3d65c68e4051e9f14d0ed2567b847","body":{"detail":"Rate cards now apply on their own (POST /api/admin/pricing/models), but PUT /api/admin/pricing still takes the whole line set (crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs set_pricing: a line left out is deleted, every line given is rewritten). Two tabs or two admins: A loads Pricing, B saves a card or prices a model from tokenulator.dev, A changes the free tier and clicks Save: B's token lines are rewritten to A's stale copy, or deleted if B added the model. Nothing versions the lines, so neither side is told.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"2df804a3aaa38450bafbadd7b0914c90f90642576a4087be85f0880d8d499845"},"suggested_fix":"Let PUT /api/admin/pricing leave token lines (unit mtok_*) alone, keeping any it is not given, and have the page send only the non-token lines; or version the line set and refuse a stale PUT with 409.","summary":"Save sends back every token line as this page read it, so another admin's rate-card change made since then is reverted by an unrelated Save (a margin or the free tier)","tags":["review","pricing","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404239Z","id":"24e24087777f792a8a4296f06c449d0c80bacb1e2aa7e2944ee029a922af2f03","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"640b22a586f390846449fadd6d4eba2e978649df58019630087ab8cafa41b811","summary":"Worth fixing before merge: the shell confirms comparable destructive actions with confirm() (web/shell/src/bot/KeyField.svelte:35 'ClaxBot stops using it at once'), and Remove can change charging at once for a tier model: with require_explicit_price on, removing the default tier's card refuses every run on it; otherwise it silently moves to the default rates, an estimate. The page can say which before the click (m.listing and the strict switch give catalog / default / refused): confirm(`Remove the rates set for ${m.model}? Its tokens are then charged at ${...}.`), and add a test that a declined confirm sends no DELETE.","tags":["review","pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404310Z","id":"16059b84ba296762289957e1e1be271e3a5a98141951f78c1f4faec55ff3dc43","body":{"detail":"The drift flag names only the drifted units' costs, but the button calls POST /api/admin/pricing/tokenulator, which sets all four lines at TOKEN_MARGIN_BP (crates/clax-server/src/routes/admin.rs price_from_tokenulator). An admin who set a 60 % margin, or fixed credits on output, to correct a drifted input cost loses those choices.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":164},"content_hash":"3cc0e77da9ef9c25946a9b76a394ab5fdf372355d856ac58bfbc304b8b2f6d0a"},"suggested_fix":"Say it in the button or a confirm ('Reprice all four units at tokenulator.dev's cost plus 40 %'), or offer 'Use its costs' that opens the editor with the catalog's costs filled in and the card's margins and fixed units kept.","summary":"'Use tokenulator.dev's price' replaces the whole rate card, resetting every unit's margin to the token margin and turning fixed-credit units cost-based, on one click and without saying so","tags":["review","pricing","ux","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404355Z","id":"4ec0c8017f9462fbddcca0062d9088ce05a9f0c170316b03260f1e891bc6c1d7","body":{"detail":"err renders above the Credits section (line 136) while Save and its status are at lines 251-254, below Models, Add a model, Default rates and Other cost lines. A refused Save looks like nothing happened unless the admin scrolls up; the role=alert announces it to a screen reader but not to the eye.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"2022eb612237b7ed6dc28c38ec887b21cb1493384afec8caf05cdd4c56136271"},"suggested_fix":"Show save()'s err in the Save row (role=alert) and keep the top message for the load failure only.","summary":"Save's errors (a bad credit price, free tier or default rate, or a refusal) show at the top of a five-section page, out of view of the Save button at the bottom","tags":["review","pricing","ux","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404398Z","id":"9bed5ef0dbe5904765e536a9fd709caee349f8a12fdb672ecb349b36d15b50f2","body":{"detail":"RateCard takes focus on open (RateCard.svelte:30), but on close the editor row unmounts and nothing returns focus to the row's Edit button; after Remove, hasLine(m) turns false and the focused button disappears. Keyboard and screen-reader users land at the top of the document.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"b75c8dde1ffc6af31db34ee4a83623374439191c5f85b37eb2175f695c1b7770"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a ref per row's Edit button and focus it after saveCard()/onCancel and after a successful remove; test document.activeElement after Cancel.","summary":"Focus is dropped to the body when the rate-card editor closes (Save rates, Cancel) and when Remove succeeds (its button is removed)","tags":["review","pricing","a11y","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404438Z","id":"fa22d3d13e8eed0050fe13b3de0e5073f398cbc17b2f3b3d339cf4374b01b23e","body":{"detail":".pr { min-width: 680px } (line 261) applies to .pr-m, and the editor is a colspan row of it. On a 375px viewport the card is laid out at 680px+ inside .scroll: the admin scrolls sideways to reach the fourth unit and the Save button, while the RateCard's own grid (RateCard.svelte:94, minmax(200px, 1fr)) would stack to one column if given the viewport's width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":181},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"862fd44e2a82918140819679ef862537948306d787e759a46522098874e78f9a"},"suggested_fix":"Render the open editor outside the table (below it, labelled by the model), or give .pr-edit > td position: sticky; left: 0 with a viewport-bounded width.","summary":"The rate-card editor renders inside the models table, whose min-width is 680px, so at phone width the four unit fieldsets and Save rates sit in a horizontally scrolled cell","tags":["review","pricing","ux","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404494Z","id":"ad805e7f7292cd32cb701ee0799b8e82c3267d0ed144f112c57d1a254a26a86a","body":{"detail":"RateSource::is_estimated (crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs:409) is true for catalog and default, and usage views follow it, but RATE_SOURCES labels catalog 'tokenulator.dev' and default 'default rate, estimated', and ModelSelect's note (ModelSelect.svelte:48) warns only for default. An admin reading Usage sees 'estimated' on rows this page presents as a firm price. Separately, a line written by 'Look up and price' badges 'set', the same as one typed by hand; its CostLine.source names tokenulator.dev. Every unit cell repeats the badge (AdminPricing.svelte:172), so four identical badges per row are the common case.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"56d3b9a502c2a37cabfbe7bbed4370c3ba767b0c493bdc9a9c9670d27807d994"},"suggested_fix":"Pick one meaning of 'estimated' for page, picker and usage (catalog included or not) and word the badges from it; show the line's own source as the badge's title for 'set'; show one badge per row when the four units agree.","summary":"The UI calls only default-sourced rates 'estimated', while the store and the design call catalog-sourced charges estimated too; and a line priced from tokenulator.dev badges as 'set'","tags":["review","pricing","ux","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/RateCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404537Z","id":"731c17bf5afb18ca271ca7a1ef73b5bee3130ad522f415891b5bb89704cb4222","body":{"detail":"draft() takes margin from u.margin_bp ?? TOKEN_MARGIN_BP, but the default rates resolve with margin_bp 0 and cost 0 (crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs:673-681), not null. Editing acme-small-2 (all default) and choosing Cost + margin shows margin 0, unlike 'Add a model', which starts at 40.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"054a4f32196b1b0cf62b6d6c3ab33d36c3e8156bfa31e96110e747482e30c99e"},"suggested_fix":"Start margin at TOKEN_MARGIN_BP unless the unit is cost-based (fixed_credits_milli null); test Edit on a defaultPriced model.","summary":"A unit at the default rates (or any fixed unit) starts the editor at a 0 % margin, so switching it to Cost + margin begins at $0 + 0 % rather than the token margin","tags":["review","pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404578Z","id":"c8077a19fddb065d3e419e0513a77ef39afc855f7b9e232cb0a0f87283347d4a","body":{"detail":"priceMicro derives from the unsaved 'Credit price (USD)' input (line 49). With an edited, unsaved price, the editor's '= N credits per million tokens' disagrees with the row it edits, and 'Save rates' charges at the saved price.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"68ffdca2a42719f3ea50db85aa13b6ff51903ad03467cdb731d4db8519785841"},"suggested_fix":"Pass p.credit_price_micro_usd to RateCard (here and at line 212).","summary":"The rate card's preview uses the credit price typed in the form but not saved, while the models table shows credits at the saved price","tags":["review","pricing","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404611Z","id":"1397d94651064e5e05290d7aaaca3427c6c107bf1cd4f842b1fcac08c39e324d","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"0cafa4d59d7011663eb57d03dbd8fa453fbc62408ab0f26000877cd8e04f353e"},"suggested_fix":"Track which action is busy, or label it from a flag add() sets.","summary":"'Look up and price' reads 'Looking up…' whenever any model action is in flight (Refresh, Remove, Save rates), not only its own","tags":["review","pricing","ux","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404648Z","id":"4f36ec9093cd37fa1be4d875c712d0f54287dc0cccf0054a35b26359ebefcc7f","body":{"detail":"Store token line IDs are '{model}.{unit}' (crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs token_line), and a model whose four units are source line has four lines in `lines`. The admin tests therefore never exercise Save sending four token lines, nameOf with a real line set, or a response whose `lines` dropped a removed model's lines (admin.test.ts 'removes a model's rate card'). Missing tests besides: Save after a card save sends the response's token lines; Save while a card POST is pending (see the concern at AdminPricing.svelte:53); Edit on a default-priced model; nameOf falling back to listing.name; Cancel returning focus.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":223}},"suggested_fix":"Build pricing().lines from modelPricing() with token_line IDs and '{name} {what} tokens' labels for all four units, make the Remove fixture drop them, and add the tests listed.","summary":"pricing() is not what GET /api/admin/pricing answers: its one token line is 'sonnet-in' while modelPricing() claims four line-sourced units, and the Remove test's 'after' keeps the deleted line","tags":["review","pricing","tests","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:39:39.404736Z","id":"44039f58b86b4227799cf430e8f230bce3b466d66e3d943b3d6db9c394462d2a","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"336a51591cae7f97b3c907def7a5ee936a99fdf733736b9dfc1e1d6a33e19f35"},"suggested_fix":"Rewrap the comment.","summary":"The header comment's new clause is one 128-character line; the rest of the comment wraps at 72-74","tags":["review","style","session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:47:23.086470Z","id":"4294dc64d06c7a9f419a7100193ac6e22e309d8553b980d53f1ea0a9caadfdf7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a4c083eaf3673774594153819ad746fad5720b85f1c741356aee8eb02afca7cb","summary":"Fixed in 998ba1bab: every write on the page (Save, a rate card, Remove, a catalog price, Refresh, a lookup) goes through write(), which refuses while `busy` holds another; Save is aria-disabled meanwhile. Test: 'runs one write at a time: Save waits for a rate card in flight, and only the busy action says so' in web/shell/src/bot/admin.test.ts (//web:unit passed).","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:47:23.087534Z","id":"0ebd1b10b559726cd42fc08190e3bb9ac119b7d9209fd8f38b9e3391878b0422","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dfdb87020b421fb18db0e82cb9bb4ab453f3d65c68e4051e9f14d0ed2567b847","summary":"Fixed in 998ba1bab: Save sends only the non-token lines (`others`), as PUT /api/admin/pricing takes them once it refuses token lines. Tests: the Save test and the one-write-at-a-time test assert the PUT's lines are ['compute', 'harness'].","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:47:23.088463Z","id":"2ac4ebd0b63cd49f08541790a15faaa983ad0392fa5ddc8e262a1d19bc832460","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"db9fc50fb07e8ff102c5d5f10995aad66f86214724656b6a6199e7ae0d0973df","summary":"Fixed in 998ba1bab: nameOf is gone; an Edit leaves `name` out (POST /api/admin/pricing/models keeps the lines' name) and the row shows `models[].name`. Tests: the edit tests assert the POST body has no `name`.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/bot/AdminPricing.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-01T22:47:23.089372Z","id":"029e945c52ba43a37b0e9c44a2bb492ff53e3fffa965c0895cd163193aa804da","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"640b22a586f390846449fadd6d4eba2e978649df58019630087ab8cafa41b811","summary":"Fixed in 998ba1bab: Remove asks confirm() naming what charges the model next (tokenulator.dev's price, the default rates, or refused under require_explicit_price). Tests: 'removes a model's rate card once confirmed…' (a declined confirm sends no DELETE) and 'warns that removing a card refuses runs…'.","tags":["session:claude-code:f97e2315-5ffc-47c7-94a0-050e4e7b9835"]}}
